body: "## Failure boundary\n\nThe tracker-mode linked-test sandbox copies or derives non-trivial workspace settings and must record the exact final settings document in the workspace history stream. The current seeding path writes a settings history event whose replayed document is empty, so strict history-drift validation correctly rejects the sandbox.\n\n## Repair constraints\n\n- Preserve sandbox isolation and never read or write the real project tracker during the linked command.\n- Build the final settings document once and use that same value for disk persistence and the immutable workspace history event.\n- Cover default and non-trivial settings, schema and tracker context modes, nested strict validation, repeated seeding, and deterministic replay.\n- Add a negative control that restores the empty history document and proves the gate fails."
